==Enemy==
Crazed Titan Cat is a strong enemy, with lots of health, significant range, a few knockbacks, high damage and constant attacks. He has a 40% chance to slow cats, 100% chance to cause knockback but most importantly has 15% chance to produce a level 7 [[Wave Attack]]. Whenever it fires off, it will destroy or gravely damage everything that isn't Immune to Waves. Those that survive will be knocked back and sometimes be slowed for a long time. His only weakness is his somewhat slow attack animation.

==Strategy==
Crazed Titan Cat has ridiculous amounts of health and attack power, and a dangerously high chance to create a wave. The wave length is level 7, so not even [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hacker Cat]] can outrange it, making him rather useless. High health fighters such as [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Fish Cat]] are recommended due to their outstanding cost efficiency. However, Crazed Titan Cat also has the ability to knockback and slow, which makes it rather risky to confront him in short range melee.

Crazed Titan Cat has 320 range, meaning that [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris/Cyborg Cat]] can outrange him, eventually stacking up lots of damage from their low recharge time. However, you'll need a way to deal with his waves, such as [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] or any other [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Blockers]], as otherwise these attackers will immediately perish as soon as a wave spawns.

